    "text": "Case logic says that to make a good horror game you need: Easy and clear directions Puzzles (if there are any) that are not too easy and not so hard you spend 20 minutes doing it and saves in case the game crashes And the most important one, tension, this can be done pretty easily with just simple and smart lighting and environment. Otherwise you would just be playing something maybe thrilling (if you can call it that) thats more for fun than anything.",
